From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] vaapi: report YUV420 for the 10-bit profiles too

Chromium's VA-API wrapper checks VA_RT_FORMAT_YUV420 for HEVC Main10
(only VP9 profile 2 asks for YUV420_10) and leaves the profile out of
its supported list when the check fails. Report both RT formats for the
10-bit profiles; the surface format still follows the format the client
asks for in vaCreateSurfaces.

Found by TheMojoMan in the erhai port (oneplus-erhai-ubuntu,
oneplus-erhai-video); re-implemented here.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vaapi/vaapi_config.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/vaapi/vaapi_config.c b/src/vaapi/vaapi_config.c
index ea504ef..8a57c78 100644
--- a/src/vaapi/vaapi_config.c
+++ b/src/vaapi/vaapi_config.c
@@ -21,8 +21,12 @@ vpu_profile_fourcc(VAProfile profile)
 unsigned int
 vpu_profile_rt_format(VAProfile profile)
 {
+	/* Chromium checks VA_RT_FORMAT_YUV420 for HEVC Main10 (only VP9
+	 * profile 2 asks for YUV420_10) and drops the profile otherwise,
+	 * so the 10-bit profiles report both formats. */
 	return vpu_profile_is_10bit(profile) ?
-		VA_RT_FORMAT_YUV420_10 : VA_RT_FORMAT_YUV420;
+		(VA_RT_FORMAT_YUV420 | VA_RT_FORMAT_YUV420_10) :
+		VA_RT_FORMAT_YUV420;
 }
 
 int
